<description>
Slide multi-color sprites to align their marker pixels with matching isolated border anchors.

Input structure:
- bg = most common color.
- Multi-color sprites in the interior; each has a minority-color "marker" pixel.
- Isolated border pixels (non-bg with all 4-neighbors bg) act as anchors.

Rule:
- Match each sprite to the border anchor sharing its marker color.
- Top/bottom-edge anchor (non-corner): slide sprite horizontally so marker column = anchor column.
- Left/right-edge anchor (or corner): slide sprite vertically so marker row = anchor row.

Key insight: The anchor's edge position determines the slide axis — top/bottom means horizontal, left/right (or corner) means vertical.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "multi-color sprite s with a unique marker color (minority color inside s)",
  "dst": "align to isolated border pixel d (same marker color)",
  "match_cond": "s.marker.color == d.color",
  "transform": "translate s: if d on top/bottom edge → align col(s.marker) to col(d); else → align row(s.marker) to row(d); clip out-of-bounds pixels"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  task_type: move_to_match (translate sprites to align marker pixel with matching border anchor)
  grid:
    size: 10-22 rows x 8-22 cols (aspect roughly rectangular, one side 10-14, other 18-22 [observed])
    bg: most common color (any color 1-8)
  anchor (dst):
    count: 1-3 distinct colors, each a single isolated border pixel
    placement: lies on a border row/col (top/bottom/left/right); not a corner [observed]
    isolation: all 4-neighbors equal bg (no other non-bg touching within Manhattan-1 or diagonal)
    axis_rule: top/bottom edge => sprite slides horizontally (match column); left/right edge => slides vertically (match row)
    duplicate_anchors: a color may appear at 2 opposite-edge anchors (same row/col) [observed, test only]
  sprite (src):
    count: 3-5 multi-color connected components in the interior
    colors_per_sprite: 2 (one body color + one marker color); rarely 3 [observed, 1 case]
    marker: exactly 1 pixel, color = least-frequent color inside sprite, must match one anchor color
    body: 4-13 cells of a single non-bg, non-marker color; irregular shape (hollow rect, plus, L, ring, etc.); bounding box 2x3 to 5x7
    marker_position: adjacent (4-neighbor) to body cells, typically on body perimeter or inside hollow; never isolated from body
    connectivity: 8-connected component; interior of sprite may contain bg cells (hollow)
    placement: fully inside grid; sprites do not touch each other or anchors (gap >=1 bg on all sides)
    symmetry: body often has LR or UD symmetry [observed, ~60%]
  extras:
    distractor_singletons: occasionally isolated interior pixels sharing an anchor color act as extra "mini-sprites" that also slide [observed, test_0 only]
    marker_anchor_match: every sprite's marker color must equal some anchor color; multiple sprites may share the same marker color
  transform:
    per_sprite: translate by (dr, dc) so marker aligns with anchor along the axis dictated by anchor edge
    clipping: out-of-bounds pixels after slide are dropped; bg cells under destination are overwritten; non-bg collisions are NOT overwritten
    originals_cleared: source cells become bg; anchors stay in place
  example_layout: |
    ... ... (scatter sprites in interior; each marker color matches one border anchor)
    .888.....
    .848.....    <- sprite marker=4 matches bottom anchor at col 5
    .........
    ....4....    <- bottom anchor (non-corner border)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first (build settled/aligned state, then invert by scattering sprites away from anchors)
  steps:
    - Choose grid H in [10,22], W in [8,22]; pick bg in [1..8].
    - Choose 1-3 anchor colors (distinct from bg). For each: place a single isolated non-corner border pixel (top/bottom => horizontal-axis anchor; left/right => vertical-axis anchor). Ensure 8-neighborhood (within grid) is all bg.
    - Decide number of sprites N in [3,5]; assign each a marker color from the anchor color set (multiple sprites may share a color).
    - For each sprite, build body in the OUTPUT position (aligned with anchor):
        * Pick a body color (distinct from bg and marker and other sprites' bodies when possible).
        * Generate an irregular small shape (size 4-13, bbox up to 5x7); shape types: hollow rect/ring, plus, L, T, frame-with-gap. Prefer LR or UD symmetry ~60% of the time.
        * Place marker as 1 pixel 4-adjacent to body (perimeter or inside hollow).
        * Position sprite so marker cell equals (anchor_row, chosen_col) for top/bottom anchors, or (chosen_row, anchor_col) for left/right anchors. The "free" axis coordinate is chosen so the sprite fits (with optional partial clipping OK but keep body mostly inside).
        * Ensure sprite body and marker do not touch (8-neighbor) any anchor, any other sprite, or the border (leave >=1 bg gap except where slide clips allowed).
    - Optional (10-20% of grids): add 1-4 distractor singleton pixels of one anchor color scattered in interior (each isolated 8-neighbor), same color as a left/right anchor (they also slide vertically).
    - Invert: for each sprite (and distractor), pick a scatter displacement along the OPPOSITE axis of its slide (horizontal anchors => move sprite vertically away; vertical anchors => move horizontally away) by some random nonzero offset, keeping sprite inside grid and non-overlapping. Remove original aligned sprite pixels (set to bg), paste at scattered location. This yields the input.
    - Self-check: verify by running solver that solver(input) == output.
```
